  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.10016v1</id>
    <title>Pixie: A Context-Aware Multi-Agent Multi-Modal Large Language Models (LLM) Architecture for Digital Marketing</title>
    <updated>2026-11-04T18:27:52Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.10016v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.10016v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We present Pixie, a context-aware, multi-agent large language model (LLM) architecture designed to enhance digital marketing operations across real-time and offline activities. Pixie uses a primary orchestration agent alongside task-specific and reconciliation/reviewer agents to support a broad range of marketing tasks. These agents combine zero-shot and few-shot prompting with marketing data, proprietary expert strategy guidelines, and documentation for proprietary statistical models.
  We experiment with agentic workflows ranging from single-agent to multi-agent systems. We evaluate them using assessments by trained marketing experts and measurements of LLM output variance, focusing on accuracy, consistency, and domain-specific problem-solving. Results show that Pixie's multi-agent framework improves decision quality and operational efficiency in digital marketing workflows.
  We assess Pixie on common digital marketing processes, including root-cause analysis and reporting, campaign research, and planning. The framework is designed to support additional specialized agents for other marketing tasks and adapt to evolving digital marketing needs.</summary>
    <category term="cs.MA" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-04T18:27:52Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>7 pages; Presented at the AIM Machine Learning Developers Summit (MLDS 2025). All authors contributed equally</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.MA"/>
    <arxiv:journal_ref>Lattice Journal, Association of Data Scientists (ADaSci), Vol. 6, Issue 2, February 2025</arxiv:journal_ref>
